    "created_at": "2016-03-28T22:18:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-28T22:18:46Z",
    "body": "Whoops, yeah, I forgot about that special counter-increment behavior.\n\ncounter-reset isn't the right way to handle this; it does happen to accomplish the goal, but it has side-effects (tho they're not visible in normal/valid HTML).  The right thing to do is deal with the increment directly; per spec, `summary { counter-increment: list-item 0; }` will have the correct effect.\n\n(This is actually a minor, but valid, argument in favor of creating a new `display` value that just creates a marker.  This counter-increment behavior means we really are, in a small way, giving `display: list-item` the semantic of \"list item\".)\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
